# Symbulator circuit book

title: Circuits for Lesson 6 of the Tutorial (Part 3)

[Bo2's Figure 5.38 (Impulse)]

j,0,1,i*δ(t)
c,1,0,c,0
r,1,0,r

analysis: tr
note: In this problem, we use an impulse source, i*δ(t), for the first time. Find the capacitor's voltage drop and current. The impulse survives in the capacitor's current, which is right: the charge arrives all at once.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/bo2s-figure-5-38-impulse-27.jpg [506px]
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


