[Bo2's Example 6.2 (DC, the left half)]

e,0,1,7/2
r1,1,2,4
c,2,0,2
r2,2,0,1/6

analysis: dc
note: For t < 0 the switches split this circuit in two. The left half's DC solve gives the capacitor's initial condition, -7/50 V — solved in fractions on purpose.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/bo2s-example-6-2-33.jpg
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


[Bo2's Example 6.2 (DC, the right half)]

r3,3,0,1/6
l,3,0,1/50
r4,3,4,3
e2,4,0,3

analysis: dc
note: The right half's DC solve gives the inductor's initial condition, 1 A.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/bo2s-example-6-2-33.jpg
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


[Bo2's Example 6.2 (TR, both halves joined)]

c,1,0,2,-7/50
r,1,0,[1/6,1/6]
l,1,0,1/50,1

analysis: tr
note: The TR interval, both halves joined: find vc and il — underdamped now, decaying sinusoids in cos(4t) and sin(4t). The switch on the right is simulated as a short between the two halves, which saves renaming every node.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/bo2s-example-6-2-33.jpg
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes
